# UIMi kit vs product UI

`index.html` is a **preview catalog**, not a finished product. When adapting UIMi into an app (or when another Cursor session uses this repo as a reference), copy **kit pieces**, never the whole demo shell.

## Never copy (authoring / studio chrome)

These are design tools for editing the kit. They are **not** theme UI and must **not** appear in product layouts:

- `.uimi-studio` — Design bar (theme/font/usage selects, Paint, Move, Glass)
- `.uimi-paint-pop`, `.uimi-glass-gear`, `.uimi-glass-modal` — injected paint/glass editors
- `.uimi-copy-fab`, `[data-uimi-copy-page]`, `.uimi-snippet`, `.uimi-note` — catalog helpers
- Anything marked `data-uimi-kit="authoring"`

Theme **controls** (palette / font dropdowns) ≠ the theme itself. The theme is only:

- `uimi.css`
- `data-uimi-palette`, `data-uimi-font`, `data-uimi-display`, `data-uimi-shell` on `<html>`

## Liquid Glass is not a theme

Do not duplicate palettes into “LG” and “non-LG” themes. Glass is a separate preference (iPhone-like on/off):

- Theme: `data-uimi-palette` / font / shell
- Glass: `data-uimi-glass="on"` or `"off"` on `<html>`, plus `.uimi-glass` on chosen surfaces when on
- Same Apricot (or any palette) can power a solid app and a glass app

Studio Off/On + gear + modal = authoring only — never ship those.

**How to choose glass:**

1. User says no glass / solid → `data-uimi-glass="off"`.
2. User asks for liquid glass → `on` + `.uimi-glass` on chosen surfaces.
3. Named preset → use it; else if glass wanted → **Regular**.
4. Glass not mentioned → **Off**. Do not add glass unprompted.
5. Never apply Regular + Clear + Chrome + Thick together — one preset.

## Catalog shell is also not product

The top navbar / sidebar that lists **Login 1, Login 2, Dashboard 1–3, Buttons…** is catalog navigation. Do not ship it as the product chrome.

**Never ship the UIMi logo.** `.uimi-kit-mark` and `icons/letter-u.png` are kit branding only. Product apps use their own mark inside a plain `.uimi-mark` (or drop the mark). If you paste catalog chrome, strip `data-uimi-kit="catalog"`, `.uimi-kit-mark`, and the “UIMi” wordmark.

## Pick one variant per family (how to choose)

Multiple pages/blocks are **reference options**, not screens to ship together. Never paste Login 1 + Login 2, or every table freeze demo, into one product.

**Decision order:**

1. **User named it** → use that (`login-2`, “freeze header table”, Dashboard 3, pill buttons).
2. **User did not name it** → ask once, briefly (e.g. “Login 1 or Login 2?”). Do not start building all of them.
3. **User says pick / defaults / just build** → use the catalog default (`*-1` or the first simple pattern).

| Family | Options | Default if user says “pick” |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Login | `login-1`, `login-2` | `login-1` |
| Dashboard | `dashboard-1`, `dashboard-2`, `dashboard-3` | `dashboard-1` |
| Buttons | rounded / square / pill / `uimi-btn--oval` (catalog `#buttons` 2×2) | rounded |
| Tables | plain wrap · freeze-head · freeze-col · freeze-head+cols | plain `.uimi-table-wrap` unless they need sticky scroll |
| Cards / forms / tabs / … | several demos on one page | first / simplest pattern that matches the job |

Pages: `.uimi-page[data-uimi-page="…"]`. On multi-demo pages (tables, cards), copy **one** block, not the whole page of examples. Prefer Usage/Copy over cloning `index.html`.

## Correct product extract

1. Link / import `uimi.css` (and icons/fonts as needed).
2. Set theme attrs on `<html>` (or the app root).
3. Take markup from **one** chosen page / component pattern.
4. Strip authoring nodes and catalog-only notes/snippets.
5. Swap demo copy and the UIMi brand for the real product.

If you catch yourself outputting `.uimi-studio`, Paint/Move/Glass controls, or Login 1 **and** Login 2 in the same product screen, stop and remove them.
